invariant: INV-14
file: webpki_ticket.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh webpki_ticket
reason: the ticket shape accepts a PSK of any non-zero length, though
  ks_res_psk writes exactly a suite's hash length, SHA256_LEN in this
  build. Through an init call hspost_present_ticket refuses that length
  first, so no session test sees this rule: webpki_resume_test's
  one-short and one-over rows pass with it broken. The webpki_ticket
  harness calls webpki_resumption_ok directly, and its stated shape
  requires SHA256_LEN.

--- old
    return psk_len == SHA256_LEN;
--- new
    return psk_len > 0;
